/ A where compared to an unset %variable% is an error (VariableNotFound), never a quietly empty list —
/ the value is the developer's own variable, read when the step runs. (Was ListTests.Where_OrderedByAnUnsetVariable.)
Start
- variable.set(Name=%users%, Value=[{name: "a", age: 30}, {name: "b", age: 10}])
- list.query(List=%users%, Query={where: {field: "age", op: ">", value: %limit%}}); on.error(Recovery=[goal.call(Name="Caught")]); variable.set(Name=%kept%, Value=%!data%)
- assert.isNotNull(Value=%caught%, Message="a where compared to an unset variable is an error, not a quietly empty list")

Caught
- variable.set(Name=%caught%, Value=%!error.Message%)
